    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d649">

                <pb facs="0760" n="658" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg658"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.003/564: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-28T20:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 28, 1919, 8
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 29, 8.15
                            a.m.</hi>]<anchor n="82" xml:id="d649-f1"/></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your May 21st [<hi rendition="#italic">22d</hi>], 2 p.m. Arnold states that
                    delegates Tariff Revision Commission did not sign draft revised tariff, as some
                    feared they would thereby prematurely commit their Governments. Printed draft
                    and printed appendix, as forwarded Arnold’s despatch of <pb facs="0761" n="659"
                        xml:id="pg659"/> April 3rd, to the Department, authentic. Foreign Office
                    will cable Chinese Legation authorizing acceptance printed draft forwarded by
                    Arnold as the basis for convention and empowering Chargé d’Affaires to sign.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
